%% AuthenticSelf - AR-furniture-placement: ARPlacementScreen state machine
%% Five values of `status` + a paired `errorCode` for the error branch.
%% Source-of-truth enum (src/mobile/src/screens/ARPlacementScreen.tsx:122):
%%   type ARStatus = 'loading' | 'live' | 'placed' | 'cancelled' | 'error';
%%
%% Design.md §5 used 'live' (matches source); some task-brief drafts wrote
%% 'ar_active' / 'committed' / 'not_supported'. This diagram follows the
%% SOURCE enum; the mapping is called out in the README delta list.
%%
%% Transitions are triggered by outbound bridge messages (decodeOutbound
%% from bridge.ts) OR by the teardown useEffect. Every transition is
%% pinned to the AC that exercises it.
%%
%% FR / AC anchors:
%%   FR-5 (shell)           FR-6 (error)     FR-7 (placed + Alert)
%%   FR-8 (cancelled)       FR-10 (teardown) AC-21 / AC-22 / AC-25..AC-32

stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> loading : mount with<br/>route.params = { roomId, item }<br/>FR-5

    loading --> live : useEffect on mount<br/>setStatus('live') + webviewRef.inject(loadPayload)<br/>renders testID='ar-webview'<br/>AC-21

    live --> placed : onMessage({event:'placed', pose})<br/>via decodeOutbound<br/>handlePlaced → emitArFurniturePlaced(...)<br/>Alert.alert('배치 완료', ...)<br/>FR-7 / AC-22 / AC-23 / AC-30

    live --> cancelled : onMessage({event:'cancelled'})<br/>handleCancelled → navigation.goBack()<br/>(NO Alert, NO addToWishlist call)<br/>FR-8 / AC-25

    live --> error : onMessage({event:'error', errorCode})<br/>OR ARWebView.onDecodeError<br/>→ handleError(code)<br/>setErrorCode + setStatus('error')<br/>FR-6 / AC-26 / AC-27

    placed --> [*] : Alert dismissal (either button)<br/>navigation.goBack() → screen unmount<br/>TEARDOWN useEffect injects unload message<br/>AC-28 / AC-29<br/>(ONE-WAY: no recovery within-screen)

    cancelled --> [*] : already dispatched goBack()<br/>unmount fires teardown useEffect<br/>AC-29<br/>(ONE-WAY)

    error --> [*] : user taps [돌아가기] (testID=btn-ar-back)<br/>→ navigation.goBack() → unmount<br/>teardown useEffect injects unload<br/>AC-32 / AC-29<br/>(ONE-WAY: no retry, no recovery)

    note right of loading
        Transient - collapses to 'live' on
        the same tick as the mount useEffect.
        The WebView IS mounted during 'loading'
        (the ref is populated by first render),
        so AC-21 passes under 'live'.
    end note

    note right of live
        WebView (testID=ar-webview) mounted.
        btnPlace disabled until model-viewer
        fires its 'load' event inside the
        HTML scene (AC-27 tests that on
        'error' transition, ar-webview
        DISAPPEARS - the fallback panel
        renders the inlined branch instead).
    end note

    note right of placed
        Transient - Alert's button callback
        synchronously calls navigation.goBack().
        State is observable by tests because
        setStatus('placed') runs BEFORE
        Alert.alert is invoked (AC-22).
        emitArFurniturePlaced fires exactly
        once here (AC-30), BEFORE the wishlist
        branch so analytics fire regardless
        of button choice.
    end note

    note right of error
        Terminal until goBack().
        ar-webview UNMOUNTED (AC-27).
        ar-fallback MOUNTED with:
          - Text: AR_ERROR_COPY[errorCode]
          - Pressable testID='btn-ar-back'
            accessibilityLabel='돌아가기'
            accessibilityRole='button' (AC-39)
        Four errorCode values (AC-26):
          AR_NOT_SUPPORTED
          AR_CAMERA_DENIED
          AR_MODEL_LOAD_FAILED
          AR_SESSION_ERROR
    end note

    note left of cancelled
        Transient - handleCancelled is
        effectively a goBack() + setStatus
        call. Covered by AC-25: NO Alert
        fires, addToWishlist is NOT called.
    end note
